# Technical stack

- React Native with Expo for mobile app development
- Supabase for backend:
  - User authentication
  - Secure database (PostgreSQL)
  - Row-level security enabled to protect private user data
- OpenRouter (or OpenAI API) for generating emotionally supportive AI responses based on journal input
- OneSignal for cross-platform push notifications, including interactive buttons
- Local state via React Context or Redux for mood and avatar state
- Expo or react-native-voice (optional later) for converting voice to journal text
- Lottie or Animated API for simple “gift to inner child” animations
- AsyncStorage or Supabase DB for storing gift/message history

# Considerations

- No clinical/medical data is stored — journal data is private and user-controlled
- Privacy-first approach with optional deletion and no PII collection in MVP
- Easy to swap Supabase with a Flask backend in future if needed

